;; =============================================================================
;; Spec: Eliminate requiring-resolve agent-smell across the codebase
;; =============================================================================
;;
;; Standards-pack rule "No requiring-resolve in Clojure" flags 134 occurrences
;; across 10 components / bases. Per `feedback_avoid_requiring_resolve`:
;;   `requiring-resolve` is an agent-smell; fix the underlying design instead
;;   of lazy-resolving around load-order issues.
;;
;; Each call site is one of:
;;   (a) a load-order workaround for a circular `:require` (real design fix
;;       needed: restructure to break the cycle)
;;   (b) a defensive idiom for "this var might not be loaded yet" (real fix:
;;       add an eager `:require` in the consumer's ns)
;;   (c) an optional dependency the original author didn't want to declare
;;       (real fix: declare it; if truly optional, hide behind a protocol or
;;       capability flag)
;;
;; This work decomposes naturally per component / base — each cluster is
;; independent, tests run per brick, no cross-cluster ordering constraint.

{:spec/title
 "Eliminate the requiring-resolve agent-smell across the codebase (134 sites in 10 bricks)"

 :spec/description
 "Replace every `(requiring-resolve 'some.ns/some-var)` call with an eager
  `:require` in the consuming namespace (and a direct symbol reference), OR
  with a proper design fix when the original author was masking a circular
  dependency.

  Audit baseline (2026-06-04 `bb review` post-FSM-RFC): 134 production
  occurrences across `components/*/src` and `bases/*/src`, concentrated:
    bases/cli           — 28 sites
    components/workflow — 15
    components/gate     — 14
    components/agent    — 13
    components/phase    — 12
    components/web-dashboard — 10
    components/evidence-bundle — 8
    components/phase-deployment — 5
    components/operator — 4
    components/event-stream — 4

  Each cluster is independently fixable: per-brick tests verify locally, no
  cross-cluster import dependency exists today (if one shows up during work,
  that IS the load-order design issue the smell was masking and the planner
  should split the affected cluster further).

  Per `feedback_avoid_requiring_resolve`, DO NOT:
    - rewrap `requiring-resolve` in a try/catch and call it a fix;
    - introduce a `delay` around the resolve (lazy-but-still-resolve);
    - move the resolve into an init fn (still lazy-by-runtime).

  Each fix MUST root-cause one of:
    (a) Add the eager `:require` to the consumer namespace; if that creates a
        circular dep, restructure (extract shared protocol / move pure helper
        down a layer) until it doesn't.
    (b) Replace with a multimethod / protocol dispatch when the resolve was
        compensating for a missing polymorphic seam.
    (c) For truly-optional deps, hide behind an explicit capability flag the
        consumer checks at the top — not a runtime resolve buried in the
        middle of a function body."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :refactor
  :scope ["bases/cli/src"
          "components/workflow/src"
          "components/gate/src"
          "components/agent/src"
          "components/phase/src"
          "components/web-dashboard/src"
          "components/evidence-bundle/src"
          "components/phase-deployment/src"
          "components/operator/src"
          "components/event-stream/src"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["Every removed `requiring-resolve` MUST be replaced with an eager `:require` or a proper protocol/dispatch — never with a `delay`, `try/catch around resolve`, or `init-fn that resolves at boot`"
  "When a fix would create a circular `:require`, the work is to BREAK the cycle (extract shared protocol or pure helper namespace) — not to fall back to a runtime resolve"
  "Per-brick tests must stay green; integration tests touching the cluster must stay green"
  "No behavior change at runtime: this is a load-time / static-dependency cleanup"
  "Tasks are independently committable per cluster — do not bundle multiple clusters into one diff unless they share a root cycle that must be broken atomically"
  "The Polylith `:poly/interface` boundary must be respected — if a fix would import a non-interface namespace across bricks, the cycle break needs to expose the helper via the brick's interface, not reach around it"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["`grep -rE '\\(requiring-resolve' components/ bases/ --include='*.clj' | grep -v _test.clj | wc -l` returns 0 (or the residue is documented in the PR as truly-optional deps behind explicit capability flags)"
  "`bb review` post-fix shows zero remaining flags under rule 'No requiring-resolve in Clojure' on production code paths"
  "Every per-brick test suite (`clojure -M:poly test brick:<each-touched-brick>`) passes"
  "Pre-commit smoke (`bb test:precommit`) passes"
  "No new `delay`-wrapped resolves, try-catch-around-resolve patterns, or boot-time resolve helpers introduced"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :should
  :axes #{:correctness :dogfood-enabler}
  :theme :standards-cleanup
  :rationale "120+ violations of an alwaysApply standards rule. Each requiring-resolve hides a real load-order design issue and silently breaks under AOT/native-image. Cleanup is naturally parallelizable per brick — exercises the FSM RFC's multi-workflow decomposition AND removes a class of agent-smell from production."
  :blocks []
  :blocked-by []}}
